      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T22:34:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With `CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ_DRIVER` set, both `board_ap_power_action_g3_s5` and \n`board_ap_power_check_power_rails_enabled` can be included in single power state handler:\n\n```suggestion\nstatic int board_ap_power_action_g3_run(void *data)\n{\n\tif (ap_pwrseq_sm_is_event_set(data, AP_PWRSEQ_EVENT_POWER_STARTUP)) {\n\t\tpower_signal_set(PWR_EN_PP5000_A, 1);\n\t\tpower_signal_set(PWR_EN_PP3300_A, 1);\n\n\t\tupdate_ap_boot_time(ARAIL);\n\t}\n\t/* Handle `gpio_pwr_1p25v_pg` delay */\n\treturn power_signal_get(PWR_EN_PP3300_A) \u0026\u0026\n\t       power_signal_get(PWR_EN_PP5000_A) \u0026\u0026\n\t       gpio_pin_get_dt(GPIO_DT_FROM_NODELABEL(gpio_pwr_1p25v_pg));\n}\n```\nTo make this more robust, you can consider declaring `gpio_pwr_1p25v_pg` as power signal to avoid missing signal assertion.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "c7da1a7b95f2b4c5fdbb79e792c6817d77a3bede",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dfc8c361_fc3f669a",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/ocelot/ojal/src/board_power.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T22:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Correction**: AP Powe sequcne driver requires action handlers to return `0` in order to move forward. `board_ap_power_action_g3_run` must return 0 if all power signals are asserted.\n```\n\tif (power_signal_get(PWR_EN_PP3300_A) \u0026\u0026\n\t    power_signal_get(PWR_EN_PP5000_A) \u0026\u0026\n\t    gpio_pin_get_dt(GPIO_DT_FROM_NODELABEL(gpio_pwr_1p25v_pg)))\n\t\treturn 0;\n\t\n\treturn 1;\n```",
      "parentUuid": "468efe99_20e6394d",
